# ========================================
# SIF 3.7 Certification Tests - Credentials
# ========================================
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual credentials.
#
# These credentials are used by each test section's setup steps (01-create-domain,
# 02-create-solution, 03-get-admin-environment, 99-teardown) to create and delete
# the certification domain and solution. Section-specific infrastructure is managed
# using credentials derived from the solution (stored in Bruno vars by step 03).
#
# Credential Naming Pattern:
#   {currentEnv}-{role}SessionToken
#   {currentEnv}-{role}SharedSecret
#
# Where:
#   - currentEnv = value from your Bruno environment file (e.g., "cert")
#   - role = "admin" (the only role needed for domain/solution management)
#
# The admin credentials must have permission to create and delete
# domains and solutions on the target broker.

# ========================================
# Certification Environment (default)
# ========================================
# Admin credentials for domain/solution lifecycle
cert-adminSessionToken=<your-admin-session-token>
cert-adminSharedSecret=<your-admin-shared-secret>
